For each $i\in {\mathcal{H}}_0$, let $\mathcal{D}_{i}$ be the distribution of $(p'_j,1\leq j\leq m)$, where 
\[
\left\{\begin{array}{l}
p'_j=0,\ j\in{\mathcal{H}}_1,\ p'_i=1/(\ell+1);\\
p'_j,\ j\in{\mathcal{H}}_0\backslash\{i\}\ \text{are i.i.d. conditionally on }U\text{ with a common c.d.f. }F^U;\\
U=(U_1,\dots,U_{\ell+1})\text{ has i.i.d. }U(0,1)\text{ components,}
\end{array}\right.\tag{13}
\]


where $F^U$ denotes the discrete c.d.f. $F^U(x)=(1-U_{(\lfloor x(\ell+1)\rfloor+1)} ){\mathbb{1}\left\{1/(\ell+1)\leq x<1 \right\}}+{\mathbb{1}\left\{x\geq 1\right\}}$, $x\in \mathbb{R}$, and $U_{(1)}>\dots> U_{(\ell+1)}$ denote the order statistics of the vector $U$. Note that the distribution $\mathcal{D}_{i}$ only depends on $i$, $m$, $\ell$ and ${\mathcal{H}}_0$. The following general result holds.

\[
\hat{g}\in \mathop{\mathrm{arg\,min}}_{g \in \mathcal{G}}\left\{\hat{R}_\gamma(g)\::\: \hat{R}_0(g)\leq \beta + \epsilon_0\right\},\tag{26}
\]
